  "prompt_text": "This figure gives an overview of how **PRET** can be used across different material states and applications. At the center, PRET is presented as being controlled by two main strategies, **macrocyclic confinement** and **assembly confinement**, which seem to regulate the photophysical behavior of the system.\n\nAround this core, the image groups examples into three environments: a **solid amorphous state**, an **aqueous solution state**, and a **soft hydrogel state**. In the solid state, polymer-like or network structures are associated with **multicolour afterglow painting**, suggesting persistent luminescence in solid materials. In aqueous solution, several supramolecular forms such as micelle- or vesicle-like particles are shown and linked to **deep-tissue penetration imaging**, implying use in biological imaging where emission can be detected through tissue. In soft hydrogels, fibrous and cylindrical assemblies appear tied to **cell labelling and discrimination** as well as **dynamic information encryption**, indicating adaptable or responsive luminescent materials.\n\nThe colored side and bottom bars connect these states to broader functions including **photocatalysis** and **humidity sensors**. Overall, the figure emphasizes that tuning confinement and self-assembly enables PRET-based luminescent materials with diverse structures and practical uses.",
